  "notes": "{玉|たま} refers to round objects, gems, or balls. The kanji can also be read as ぎょく in some compounds.\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {目玉|めだま}: eyeball\n- {玉子|たまご}: egg (also written {卵|たまご})\n- {玉ねぎ|たまねぎ}: onion\n- {水玉|みずたま}: polka dots, water droplet\n- {玉入|たまい}れ: ball-toss game\n- {百円玉|ひゃくえんだま}: 100-yen coin\n\nEXPRESSIONS:\n- {玉|たま}に{瑕|きず}: a fly in the ointment (lit. a flaw in a gem)\n- {玉|たま}のような{肌|はだ}: flawless skin (lit. skin like a gem)\n\nREADINGS:\n- たま: native Japanese reading (round object, ball)\n- ぎょく: Sino-Japanese reading in {玉座|ぎょくざ} (throne), {宝玉|ほうぎょく} (jewel)\n\nNOTE:\nCan refer to bullets ({鉄砲玉|てっぽうだま}) in informal speech.",
